---
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import BasicProjectPage from "../../components/BasicProjectPage.astro";
import Judgment from "../../media/bunger/FTRookie_judge.png";
import PlaneCrazy from "../../media/PlaneCrazyThumbnail.png";
import PlaneEngineersThumbnail from "../../media/PlaneEngineersThumbnail.png";
import PlaneEngineersBanner from "../../media/PlaneEngineersBanner.png";
import Blocksworld from "../../media/Blocksworld.png";
import DMCA1 from "../../media/DMCA1.png";
import DMCA4 from "../../media/DMCA4.png";
import "../../styles/oecontributions.css";
import "../../styles/glightbox.min.css";
---

<BasicProjectPage title="OE Contributions" favicon={Judgment}>
    <br />
    <div id="content">
        <h2 class="chapterheader">Origins</h2>
        <p>
            As an engineering-aligned creative, I started out playing games like
            Blocksworld, a sandbox building game, at a young age. Similarly on
            the Roblox platform, I found Plane Crazy, and played it for a very
            long time. I have 2400 hours on it as of today. Disillusioned with
            the state of the game and the lack of updates, I decided to move on
            from Plane Crazy.
        </p>

        <div class="imagebar" style="height: 250px;">
            <Picture src={Blocksworld} alt="Blocksworld" loading={"eager"} />
            <Picture src={PlaneCrazy} alt="Plane Crazy" loading={"eager"} />
        </div>

        <h2 class="chapterheader">Finding Plane Engineers</h2>
        <p>
            I got bored one day and decided to look on the Roblox discover page.
            I found a game called Plane Engineers, decided to try it and I found
            the flight and impact destruction physics to be very fun.
            Furthermore, I discovered that the game had a logic system that
            allowed for control systems, and that is when I fell in love with
            the game.
        </p>
        <div class="imagebar" style="height:300px">
            <a
                href={PlaneEngineersThumbnail.src}
                data-title="Original Plane Engineers Thumbnail"
                class="glightbox"
            >
                <Picture
                    src={PlaneEngineersThumbnail}
                    alt="PE Thumbnail"
                    loading={"eager"}
                />
            </a>
            <a
                href={PlaneEngineersBanner.src}
                data-title="Plane Engineers Banner"
                class="glightbox"
            >
                <Picture
                    src={PlaneEngineersBanner}
                    alt="PE Banner"
                    loading={"eager"}
                />
            </a>
        </div>
        <h2 class="chapterheader">Initial Involvement</h2>
        <p>
            As a committed player with a lot of sandbox experience and a lot of
            feedback, I was very vocal in the community and garnered a
            reputation, soon becoming a tester. I quickly befriended the
            developers, <b>Maks_gaming</b>, <b>i3ym</b>, and
            <b>samlovebutter</b>. By request, created a plane tutorial which was
            then adopted into the game.
        </p>
        <iframe
            width="560"
            height="315"
            src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/t3BecB7mwgc"
            title="YouTube video player"
            allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
            referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
            allowfullscreen
            loading="lazy"
            style="margin-top:1.5rem;"
        >
        </iframe>
        <footer>maks changed aero and the plane is kil</footer>
        <h2 class="chapterheader">DMCA Takedowns</h2>
        <p>
            <b>Maks</b>, originally the developer of <i
                >Build A Plane To Crash (BAPTC)</i
            >, used public Toolbox assets from Roblox Studio in order to create
            BAPTC, including using Rickje's assets which were accidentally
            published to Toolbox.
            <b>Rickje139</b>, the developer of <i>Plane Crazy</i>, got <i
                >Plane Engineers</i
            >
            taken down through a DMCA claim. He claimed that Plane Engineers infringed
            on his copyright because of 'stolen assets' from Plane Crazy. Plane Engineers
            was the successor to <i>BAPTC</i>, but shares
            <b><u>no framework</u></b> with <i>BAPTC</i>, the games were not
            even written in the same language, with <i>BAPTC</i> being in
            <u>Lua</u>, and <i>Plane Engineers</i> being in <u>Typescript</u> respectively.
        </p>
        <br />
        <p>
            Players complained about the down time, which was a full 14 days to
            dispute each claim. At first, the developers opened
            <i>Test Engineers</i> to the public, but shortly after,
            <i>Test Engineers</i> was taken down with a DMCA claim. After several
            takedowns, the developers started reuploading the game from different
            accounts since their original accounts were banned because of the claims.
        </p>
        <div class="imagebar" style="height:auto">
            <a
                href={DMCA1.src}
                data-title="First DMCA"
                data-description="The first fraudulent DMCA claim used to take down Plane Engineers"
                class="glightbox"
            >
                <Picture src={DMCA1} alt="1st DMCA Claim" loading={"eager"} />
            </a>
            <a
                href={DMCA4.src}
                data-title="Fourth DMCA"
                data-description="Test Engineers was taken down after it opened to the public"
                class="glightbox"
            >
                <Picture src={DMCA4} alt="2nd DMCA Claim" loading={"eager"} />
            </a>
        </div>
        <h2 class="chapterheader">Learning How 2 Open-Source</h2>
        <p>
            The developers made the decision to make the game Open Sourced,
            allowing players to contribute.
            <br />
            <br />
            Previously, I never worked on anything other than my own personal projects
            in Roblox Studio written in Lua. In contrast, Overengineered was written
            in Typescript and managed via Github. Working on Overengineered was what
            taught me how to use Github and create pull requests. <b>i3ym</b> specifically,
            provided me with a lot of guidance through many of the issues with my
            <a href="https://github.com/anywaymachines/overengineered/pull/8">
                first PR
            </a>.
        </p>
        <h2 class="chapterheader">Now What?</h2>
        <p>
            As the <u>decision was made to give up on the Roblox platform</u>,
            the game repository was archived and no longer uploaded to the
            platform. I have stopped my contributions, and the developers are
            currently working on an off-platform sequel, free from
            <b>Rickje139</b>'s abuse of the Roblox DMCA system'. As of now, the
            details of the new game are unknown and the basic framework of the
            game is being laid out, but it is not even guaranteed that they will
            finish the sequel.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div id="info">
        <a href="https://github.com/anywaymachines">Original Developers</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/anywaymachines/overengineered">
            Original Repository (Archive)
        </a>
        <a
            style="display:block"
            href="https://github.com/FtRookie/overengineered">My Fork</a
        >
        <h2>Things I contributed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Propellant Blocks</li>
            <li>Tracer Block</li>
            <li>Proximity Scanner/Emitter</li>
            <li>Laser Block Range Extension</li>
            <li>Scale Block &#127820</li>
            <li>Different seat blocks</li>
            <li>Lamp Shapes</li>
            <li>
                <a
                    href="https://github.com/anywaymachines/overengineered/pulls?q=author%3AFtRookie"
                >
                    various other things
                </a>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</BasicProjectPage>
<script src="../../scripts/glightbox.min.js"></script>
<script src="../../scripts/oecontributions.ts"></script>
